stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
(must be a hard-hearted, selfish man. I found it different with most of) Tj T*
(the prominent men in Wall Street. Of course, if a Gould or a Vanderbilt) Tj T*
(buys up a whole railroad, he cannot very well take many people into) Tj T*
(his confidence; but these men are not what is generally called) Tj T*
(speculators?they are generals or diplomats, and they are not different in) Tj T*
(their actions from generals in warfare or diplomats in politics.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Outside of this class, I found generally, when I asked one of the) Tj T*
(prominent speculators for his opinion of the market, that he gave) Tj T*
(me his true and candid opinion of the future of the market; and the) Tj T*
(probabilities are that, if even not acting on this opinion at that very) Tj T*
(moment, his general policy was based on such a forecast of the market?s) Tj T*
(condition.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The strength of the successful speculator lies in his observing the) Tj T*
(important principle set forth by Mr. Crump on page 60 of his work.) Tj T*
(?Speculators never set sufficient value on the importance of avoiding a) Tj T*
(loss?they think only of the profits.? As it is with our money affairs) Tj T*
(when we say, ?_Look after the pence; the pounds will take care of) Tj T*
(themselves_,? so it is with speculation. Look after the losses; the) Tj T*
(profits will take care of themselves. Never refuse a profit, is a golden) Tj T*
(motto for speculators, which unhappily few of them, in their greediness,) Tj T*
(have the courage to adopt. The observance of this rule is the main cause) Tj T*
(of the success of the best speculators, and the non-observance is the) Tj T*
(cause of failure of even their confidential friends.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Very few fortunes have been made in Wall Street at one stroke. Fortunes) Tj T*
(which were made in that way were generally lost again in a very short) Tj T*
(time. Most of the long, lasting, and solid fortunes were made by a) Tj T*
(gradual accumulation of profits extending over a great many years. The) Tj T*
(beginnings of these were sometimes quite small, and, as the capital) Tj T*
(increased, larger operations were entered into.[1]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Another cause of failure is the habit of taking larger risks than the) Tj T*
(means of speculators warrant. They naturally become nervous when they) Tj T*
(begin to see their capital dwindle away, and then begin, what is called) Tj T*
(in Wall Street, to ?chip out.? Now this is the curse of the speculator,) Tj T*
(not so much on account of the loss, as on account of the demoralization) Tj T*
(it will lead him into. Of course, big losses ought to be avoided, but) Tj T*
(at the same time well based and matured operations may sometimes be) Tj T*
(temporarily upset by a temporary manipulation of the market, or by some) Tj T*
(accidents which however right themselves in a few days, and cannot) Tj T*
(seriously interrupt the natural course of the market. In such a market a) Tj T*
(nervous speculator may ?chip out? a fortune, and still be right in his) Tj T*
(views as to general conditions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I think it is better to make one loss of 5 per cent. or so, when you) Tj T*
(know you are wrong, than to make three or five losses of 1 per cent.) Tj T*
(each, when you do not know whether you are wrong or right, and in this) Tj T*
(connection Mr. Crump has very much undervalued the importance of options.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Options, if considered in their proper light, are the most important) Tj T*
ET
endstream
