(adjunct to speculation. They will enable the speculator to bridge over) Tj T*
(many difficulties, and furnish capital to speculators who know how to use) Tj T*
(them.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I do not say this simply because I am a broker in options, but because) Tj T*
(it is my honest conviction that options are cheap at almost any price,) Tj T*
(when a speculator has occasion to use them. If money is lost by buyers) Tj T*
(of options, it is because many of them are bought by people who have not) Tj T*
(sufficient reasons for doing so, and after the option has been bought,) Tj T*
(the owner does not know what to do with it. I have, for example, known) Tj T*
(people to be bulls on Lake Shore, and then go and spend money for a put) Tj T*
(in Western Union. Is it any wonder that men who do business on such) Tj T*
(principles lose money?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(That many stock brokers object to options is natural. They look out for) Tj T*
(commissions, and greatly prefer to buy and sell several times a day on) Tj T*
(stop orders or on margins, even if customers lose money thereby, rather) Tj T*
(than see them make money two or three times a year, through operations) Tj T*
(extended over periods of two or three months each.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(I do not mean to say that all stock brokers are of this kind, but) Tj T*
(if speculators recall their own experience, they will undoubtedly) Tj T*
(remember how often their broker said to them, ?Cut your losses,? if the) Tj T*
(transaction was against them, while, if the transaction showed a profit,) Tj T*
(the advice was, ?Taking profits will never make any man poorer.? All) Tj T*
(these things make commissions for the broker, and this is the object of) Tj T*
(his business.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Another reason for the unwillingness of some brokerage houses to) Tj T*
(encourage speculation against options must be found in the fact that a) Tj T*
(great many of them have not sufficiently large capital to enter upon) Tj T*
(large transactions without any other margin than the option. Although I) Tj T*
(acknowledge that it is hardly fair to ask a broker to do an unlimited) Tj T*
(amount of business based on options alone, the fact, nevertheless, exists) Tj T*
(that the strongest houses have always been glad to encourage trading) Tj T*
(against options, and only the more insignificant houses are opposed to it.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A well planned and matured operation, looking far ahead, backed by ample) Tj T*
(capital and patience, is the only way to make a fortune at the Stock) Tj T*
(Exchange, and prudence demands that in case the speculator?s idea should) Tj T*
(have been wrong, he should have a safe way for a retreat open. Options) Tj T*
(will fulfill all these demands; and no matter how expensive, if the) Tj T*
(speculator can afford it, it is the only way of speculating in a safe and) Tj T*
(reasonable manner.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There are some people who are under the impression that they know) Tj T*
(everything already, and have nothing to learn, and such may be amused,) Tj T*
(but not benefited, by reading this book; others, however, who are) Tj T*
(inclined to speculate \(and there are and always will be many of them\)) Tj T*
(cannot fail to derive great benefit from the perusal of Mr. Crump?s) Tj T*
(interesting work, and I hope I may put money in some people?s pockets) Tj T*
(or save others from ruin by sending this book forth among the American) Tj T*
ET
