(    contract is to be enforced.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    This practice of paying differences is, as I understand it,) Tj T*
(    much rarer, however, than the actual delivery of the stocks or) Tj T*
(    bonds mentioned in the contract. The courts have of late years,) Tj T*
(    with great uniformity, dealt with these contracts with the) Tj T*
(    disposition to uphold and maintain them, and have discredited) Tj T*
(    the defence of their being of the nature of a wager, and have) Tj T*
(    held the contracting parties to their agreements in the same) Tj T*
(    manner as in every other contract for which a reasonable) Tj T*
(    consideration had passed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    The decision of the Courts of this State, of Massachusetts,) Tj T*
(    Pennsylvania and Illinois, and in the Federal tribunals, where,) Tj T*
(    in one form or another, these contracts have been the subject) Tj T*
(    matter of examination, have been so uniform in that direction) Tj T*
(    that we can now regard this as settled law.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    It was only in the infancy of those larger and more complicated) Tj T*
(    mercantile transactions incident upon the development of the) Tj T*
(    modern industrial world, that doubts as to the moral aspect) Tj T*
(    of these contracts could arise. Political science proves, and) Tj T*
(    the law has followed the conclusion, that these time contracts) Tj T*
(    now form a necessary part and perform a conservative function) Tj T*
(    in the economy of a fully developed commercial life. They) Tj T*
(    are an as yet undeveloped form of insurance of values to a) Tj T*
(    purchaser, for which the purchaser pays a fair equivalent, and) Tj T*
(    in process of time such insurances must perform a larger and) Tj T*
(    more important function in the purchase of commodities or of) Tj T*
(    representatives of value which have a tendency to fluctuate) Tj T*
(    largely in price.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    For a time it was supposed that the ordinary policy of fire) Tj T*
(    insurance partook of the nature of a bet, and there was doubt) Tj T*
(    as to whether the Courts would enforce contracts of insurance,) Tj T*
(    because it looked as though the insurer was saying to a man who) Tj T*
(    wanted to have his house insured against fire, ?I will bet you) Tj T*
(    the value of you house that it does not burn down.? But we have) Tj T*
(    long since departed from this infantile mode of looking at the) Tj T*
(    situation and have learned to regard insurance as one of the) Tj T*
(    conservative elements of modern civilized life, by which heavy) Tj T*
(    losses are evenly distributed instead of coming with crushing) Tj T*
(    effect upon the persons suffering the misfortune.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    The capitalist who sells a ?put? or a ?call? performs precisely) Tj T*
(    the same function as an insurer. He receives an equivalent) Tj T*
(    therefor, and it is a means by which he can turn the securities) Tj T*
(    in his hands with an intermediate profit, without serious) Tj T*
(    risk, except that in the case of a ?call? he may be compelled) Tj T*
(    to change the character of his securities, or replace the) Tj T*
(    securities which he has called from him, and in the case of a) Tj T*
(    ?put? he may be compelled to re-acquire the securities that) Tj T*
